{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Session c70c47e9 (Copilot CLI) — resumed-crash recovery, CI remediation, and landed-ticket closure.\n\nWHAT LANDED + CLOSED THIS SESSION (all via normal completion-verify gate; NO force-close):\n- Gerrit MERGED: 1382(74a3), 1368(5968), 1383(dfe3), 1384(66af code), 1376(9305, d/42076d367e), 1386(1dbe, d394a70529). Plus earlier 1019/e39f/05cb.\n- Tickets CLOSED (AC-verified, verdicts recorded as comments): 74a3, 05cb, 1019, e39f, 5968, dfe3, 9305, 1dbe.\n- 1dbe close ran the completion gate; the tickets-branch push warned 'failed after 3 retries' but self-healed via auto-reconcile merge (tip 78ca12ad25 == origin/tickets; STATUS/COMPLETION_VERDICT/SIGNATURE/COMPACT events for 1dbe present). Verified closed+synced.\n- 1dbe note: AC2 (marked prefix byte-identical across TICKETS) was formally WITHDRAWN as unsatisfiable (prefix embeds plan by design; f81d disproved moving plan to user msg); replaced by breakpoint-at-shared-prefix AC, pinned by test_cache_prefix_breakpoint.py. 28 tests pass on merged tree.\n\nIN-FLIGHT (MINE): 1385 (ad85 'fail loudly on absent Jira Cloud creds') was Verified-1 from a STALE-BASE merge conflict in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_config_validation.py (docstring conflict between bdb8 item-2a enforcement on main and ad85 item-2b enforcement). Resolved LOCALLY in /Users/joeoakhart/wt-1385: rebased onto origin/main d394a70529, merged docstring to reflect BOTH enforcements, updated stale 'item 2b ABSENCE-DOCUMENTING' prose. 22 targeted tests pass, ruff clean, Change-Id Id09abe3 preserved. Pushed PS3 (21:22); CI run 30952075854 running; LLM-Review+1 & Verified-1 reset (real change). Land + close ad85 after green.\n\nNOT MINE — PARALLEL Claude-Code session 03d46327-27e5-406b-a8f2-adcd55335d05 owns: 1391 (fsck scoped stale-channel repair), 1392 (a092 remove tickets-pack-size Verified gate — the 561e topic), 1393 (3b5f tombstone confirmed-deleted pairing). Do NOT drive these.\n\nSTILL PENDING OPERATOR DECISION: 66af AC5 / ticket 43ea (rotate compromised GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN). BLOCKED: prod still runs pre-66af leaky code (container compose-review-bot-1, TokenRedactingFilter=0, app.py:243 URL-sourced token). Correct sequence = deploy 66af -> infra/gerrit/service-user.sh atomic rotate -> restart -> verify. Do NOT bare 'aws ssm put-parameter' (desyncs the ADR-0014 shared secret). 66af stays in_progress until rotation done.\n\nMY IDLE BG AGENTS (all merged/closed work): search-id(dfe3), cache-1dbe(1dbe), tokenleak-66af(66af), fix-1376(9305).\n\nENV NOTES: validate merged code with PYTHONPATH=<worktree>/src (shared .venv editable-installs the BEHIND main checkout). wt-close kept at origin/main for completion-gate reachability. Prefix all tooling with env PATH=.venv/bin. Stale-base tickets-pack CI failure (limit 131072 KiB) is cleared by a rebase onto current main; server-side rebase only works with no textual conflict (1385 needed a local rebase)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785879003656457001,"uuid":"9f2a35ff-5de1-443c-a08e-2719339a6cea"}